*> Smoke tests of the datamunge COBOL bindings (just test-cobol): native calls, vectors and
*> pairs, the Callback director with a COBOL override, and error propagation.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. TEST-DATAMUNGE.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge.cpy".
01 FAILURES   PIC 9(4) VALUE 0.
01 LABEL-TEXT PIC X(60).
01 V          USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 CB         USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 DOUBLER    USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 FOUND      USAGE BINARY-LONG.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    *> Smoke test: call into the native library.
    CALL "dm_hello" USING DM-HELLO DM-STATUS
    MOVE "hello" TO LABEL-TEXT
    PERFORM EXPECT-OK

    *> std::vector<double> results are handles; const references take them back.
    MOVE 1.0 TO DM-MAKE-DVECTOR-A
    MOVE 2.0 TO DM-MAKE-DVECTOR-B
    MOVE 3.0 TO DM-MAKE-DVECTOR-C
    CALL "dm_make_dvector" USING DM-MAKE-DVECTOR DM-STATUS
    MOVE DM-MAKE-DVECTOR-RESULT TO V
    MOVE V TO DM-SUM-DVECTOR-VALUES
    CALL "dm_sum_dvector" USING DM-SUM-DVECTOR DM-STATUS
    MOVE "sum_dvector = 6" TO LABEL-TEXT
    IF DM-SUM-DVECTOR-RESULT NOT = 6.0 PERFORM FAILED END-IF

    *> ... and copy to and from COBOL tables (1-based).
    MOVE V TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF
    MOVE 1 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-START
    CALL "dm_vector_double_to_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE "make_dvector = 1 2 3" TO LABEL-TEXT
    IF DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT NOT = 3 OR DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1) NOT = 1.0
            OR DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(3) NOT = 3.0
        PERFORM FAILED
    END-IF
    MOVE 2 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-COUNT
    MOVE 0.5 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(1)
    MOVE 1.5 TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-ITEM(2)
    CALL "dm_vector_double_from_table" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE DM-STATUS
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO DM-SUM-DVECTOR-VALUES
    CALL "dm_sum_dvector" USING DM-SUM-DVECTOR DM-STATUS
    MOVE "tables convert to std::vector" TO LABEL-TEXT
    IF DM-SUM-DVECTOR-RESULT NOT = 2.0 PERFORM FAILED END-IF
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-TABLE-SELF TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS

    *> std::pair<double, double> is flattened into -FIRST and -SECOND.
    MOVE 1.25 TO DM-MAKE-DPAIR-A
    MOVE 2.75 TO DM-MAKE-DPAIR-B
    CALL "dm_make_dpair" USING DM-MAKE-DPAIR DM-STATUS
    MOVE "make_dpair = 1.25 2.75" TO LABEL-TEXT
    IF DM-MAKE-DPAIR-RESULT-FIRST NOT = 1.25 OR DM-MAKE-DPAIR-RESULT-SECOND NOT = 2.75 PERFORM FAILED END-IF
    MOVE DM-MAKE-DPAIR-RESULT-FIRST TO DM-SUM-DPAIR-VALUES-FIRST
    MOVE DM-MAKE-DPAIR-RESULT-SECOND TO DM-SUM-DPAIR-VALUES-SECOND
    CALL "dm_sum_dpair" USING DM-SUM-DPAIR DM-STATUS
    MOVE "sum_dpair = 4" TO LABEL-TEXT
    IF DM-SUM-DPAIR-RESULT NOT = 4.0 PERFORM FAILED END-IF

    *> The C++ Callback (identity) passed to C++.
    CALL "dm_callback_new" USING DM-CALLBACK-NEW DM-STATUS
    MOVE DM-CALLBACK-NEW-RESULT TO CB
    MOVE 3.0 TO DM-CALL-WITH-CALLBACK-X
    MOVE CB TO DM-CALL-WITH-CALLBACK-CB
    CALL "dm_call_with_callback" USING DM-CALL-WITH-CALLBACK DM-STATUS
    MOVE "call_with_callback = 3" TO LABEL-TEXT
    IF DM-CALL-WITH-CALLBACK-RESULT NOT = 3.0 PERFORM FAILED END-IF
    MOVE V TO DM-MAP-DVECTOR-WITH-CALLBACK-VALUES
    MOVE CB TO DM-MAP-DVECTOR-WITH-CALLBACK-CB
    PERFORM MAP-AND-SUM
    MOVE "mapped sum = 6" TO LABEL-TEXT
    IF DM-SUM-DVECTOR-RESULT NOT = 6.0 PERFORM FAILED END-IF

    *> A COBOL program overrides the C++ virtual call() (a director).
    SET DM-CALLBACK-EXTEND-CALL TO ENTRY "DOUBLE-IT"
    CALL "dm_callback_extend" USING DM-CALLBACK-EXTEND DM-STATUS
    MOVE "extend" TO LABEL-TEXT
    PERFORM EXPECT-OK
    MOVE DM-CALLBACK-EXTEND-RESULT TO DOUBLER
    MOVE DOUBLER TO DM-CALL-WITH-CALLBACK-CB
    CALL "dm_call_with_callback" USING DM-CALL-WITH-CALLBACK DM-STATUS
    MOVE "COBOL override runs" TO LABEL-TEXT
    IF DM-CALL-WITH-CALLBACK-RESULT NOT = 6.0 PERFORM FAILED END-IF
    MOVE DOUBLER TO DM-MAP-DVECTOR-WITH-CALLBACK-CB
    PERFORM MAP-AND-SUM
    MOVE "mapped sum = 12" TO LABEL-TEXT
    IF DM-SUM-DVECTOR-RESULT NOT = 12.0 PERFORM FAILED END-IF

    *> A failing override reaches the caller as kind CALLBACK, with its message.
    SET DM-CALLBACK-EXTEND-CALL TO ENTRY "REFUSE-IT"
    CALL "dm_callback_extend" USING DM-CALLBACK-EXTEND DM-STATUS
    MOVE DM-CALLBACK-EXTEND-RESULT TO DM-CALL-WITH-CALLBACK-CB
    MOVE 1.0 TO DM-CALL-WITH-CALLBACK-X
    CALL "dm_call_with_callback" USING DM-CALL-WITH-CALLBACK DM-STATUS
    MOVE 0 TO FOUND
    INSPECT DM-STATUS-MESSAGE TALLYING FOUND FOR ALL "from COBOL"
    MOVE "the COBOL error propagates" TO LABEL-TEXT
    IF NOT DM-STATUS-CALLBACK OR FOUND = 0 PERFORM FAILED END-IF

    IF FAILURES = 0
        DISPLAY "test_datamunge.cob: all checks passed"
        MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE
    ELSE
        DISPLAY "test_datamunge.cob: " FAILURES " checks failed"
        MOVE 1 TO RETURN-CODE
    END-IF
    STOP RUN.

MAP-AND-SUM.
    CALL "dm_map_dvector_with_callback" USING DM-MAP-DVECTOR-WITH-CALLBACK DM-STATUS
    MOVE DM-MAP-DVECTOR-WITH-CALLBACK-RESULT TO DM-SUM-DVECTOR-VALUES
    CALL "dm_sum_dvector" USING DM-SUM-DVECTOR DM-STATUS
    MOVE DM-MAP-DVECTOR-WITH-CALLBACK-RESULT TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
    CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS.

EXPECT-OK.
    IF NOT DM-STATUS-OK PERFORM FAILED END-IF.

FAILED.
    ADD 1 TO FAILURES
    DISPLAY "FAIL " FUNCTION TRIM(LABEL-TEXT)
    IF NOT DM-STATUS-OK
        DISPLAY "  " FUNCTION TRIM(DM-STATUS-KIND) ": " DM-STATUS-MESSAGE(1:DM-STATUS-LENGTH)
    END-IF.
END PROGRAM TEST-DATAMUNGE.

*> Callback::call override: twice its argument.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. DOUBLE-IT.
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge-callbacks.cpy".
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING DM-CALLBACK-CALL-ARGS DM-CALLBACK-STATUS.
    COMPUTE DM-CALLBACK-CALL-ARGS-RESULT = 2 * DM-CALLBACK-CALL-ARGS-X
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM DOUBLE-IT.

*> Callback::call override that fails.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. REFUSE-IT.
DATA DIVISION.
LINKAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge-callbacks.cpy".
PROCEDURE DIVISION USING DM-CALLBACK-CALL-ARGS DM-CALLBACK-STATUS.
    SET DM-CALLBACK-STATUS-ARGUMENT TO TRUE
    MOVE "from COBOL" TO DM-CALLBACK-STATUS-MESSAGE
    MOVE 10 TO DM-CALLBACK-STATUS-LENGTH
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM REFUSE-IT.
